bibliograph-search (0.1.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Every request logs a span close line (`http{method=POST route=search}: close
    time.busy=…`), so the journal can answer what the service served; before
    this, a span with no events printed nothing.
  * OTLP: `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` attaches a `tracing-opentelemetry`
    layer with a blocking HTTP/protobuf exporter and a batch processor; unset
    means fmt-only, no exporter thread. Verified against a stub collector
    (`POST /v1/traces`, 473 bytes, application/x-protobuf).

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-search (0.1.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Observability: `tracing` spans and logs (journald) for every request and
    for index commits, plus `metrics` counters/histograms served from
    `GET /metrics` in Prometheus format with real histogram buckets (query and
    HTTP latency, results per query, commit duration, posts/deletes, index
    docs/segments, empty-result ratio).
  * The Grafana dashboard `bibliograph-search` (ansible role grafana) reads it.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-search (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Default bind is 127.0.0.1:3103: 3102 belongs to Loki on the host, and the
    service failed with "Address in use" there.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-search (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package: loopback Tantivy index for the catalog search.
    Ships the service and its conffile, creates the bibliograph user the
    other packages share, and keeps the index under /var/lib/bibliograph-search.
    Derived data: a rebuild from Postgres restores it.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
